<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.001 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.001 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.3 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due August 7 was 3.001 percent, down from 3.138 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 182-day T-bills due November 6, 1997 was 3.364 percent, down from 3.589 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due April 30, 1998 was 3.961 percent, down from 4.23 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$125 million one-year bills. It holds C$625 million of C$5.1 billion bills due May 15. (Details follow)  </p>
